^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.type]/1, [dcl.fct]/5: two template-ids are the same when their
type arguments are the same type; decltype(cb) and void(int) are.  A
written function type template argument keeps its parameters in parsed
form (cpp_declaration) while decltype(cb) is a converted code type, so the
instances differ (tag-W<ptr_(parameter(...))->(void)> vs
tag-W<(cpp_declaration(...))->(void)>) and the primary template is
selected.  `same<void(int), void(int)>' and pointers to functions work.
Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
